From: S4602 CI <ci@s4602.local>
Subject: [PATCH] asdl.h: use stdbool.h instead of enum bool

C23 (default on modern runners) makes false/true keywords, so
"typedef enum {false, true} bool;" fails to compile:
  Include/asdl.h:9:15: error: cannot use keyword 'false' as enumeration constant

Replace the enum with <stdbool.h> (bool/true/false identical semantics
for all users of this header in 2.7.16).
---
 Include/asdl.h | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/Include/asdl.h
+++ b/Include/asdl.h
@@ -4,9 +4,9 @@
 typedef PyObject * identifier;
 typedef PyObject * string;
 typedef PyObject * object;
 
 #ifndef __cplusplus
-typedef enum {false, true} bool;
+#include <stdbool.h>
 #endif
 
 /* It would be nice if the code generated by asdl_c.py was completely
-- 
